27 The image of anie man is the forme, wherby it repreſenteth him. A ſimilitude of anie man is a qualitie, wherein it reſembleth him. What this image then is, let vs moſt abſolutelie declare.
A man not onlie hath the power & ſtrength of vnderſtanding, whereby he is not far from God; but he is alſo created with moſt excellent and heauenlie qualities. He is indued with iuſtice, wiſdome, mercie, temperance, and charitie. But the verie full image of God, is Chriſt, as touching his diuine nature;
and further, as concerning his humane nature, ſo much as there can be of the ſimilitude of God in it: as appéereth in the firſt to the Hebrues, the firſt to the Coloſſians,
and in the eight chapter to the Romans. Againe; This is my welbeloued ſonne in whom I am well pleaſed. We were made, to the end we ſhould be ſuch: for we haue vnderſtanding, and are capable of diuine perfections. In them we were made, but we cannot be reſtored vnto them,
vnleſſe it be by the helpe and example of Chriſt, who is the principall and true image. How much we be the image of God, it appéereth by our felicitie, which we haue one and the ſame with our God; I meane, in louing and knowing. But if thou demand, by what power men rule ouer things? Doubtleſſe not by bodilie ſtrength: for as touching that, the moſt part of liuing creatures excéed vs.
Wherefore this is doone by reaſon, counſell, and art: by which man not onelie maſtereth and taketh theſe liuing creatures, but he alſo mooueth and changeth excéeding great & weightie things. This power is chéeflie reſtored by faith;
Thou ſhalt walke vpon the adder and dragon:
Pſal. 91. Daniel was caſt vnto the lions; Chriſt liued among wild beaſts in the wildernes;
Paule tooke no harme by the viper; Samſon and
Dauid ouercame the lions.
